&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking innovative, motivated recent graduates to join our team as Mechanical Engineers. In this role, you will contribute to new product development, sustainment, and engineering design projects. We are looking for someone who enjoys solving challenging problems, is thorough and detail-oriented, and uses experimentation and model-based analysis to identify root causes. You will collaborate effectively with cross-disciplinary teams to solve complex engineering problems and drive new technological advancements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design mechanical systems and products supporting ASM process chambers using sound engineering principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret and design to gas, water and pneumatic schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage 3D CAD models (Creo) and 2D drawings with GD&amp;amp;T&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform engineering analysis including structural, thermal, and fluid dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead hardware development from concept through testing and HVM readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews and drive DFx activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with suppliers to resolve fabrication challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear, complete engineering documentation to support prototype builds, manufacturing, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cost estimation for new features and enhancements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain product configuration using modern PLM tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in mechanical engineering or higher&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-3 years of experience in mechanical design using 3D CAD (Creo preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of vacuum and thermal systems, gas/fluid delivery, wafer handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of materials: QTZ; SiC; metals, surface&amp;nbsp;coatings&amp;nbsp;and surface finishes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of GD&amp;amp;T and engineering drawing standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cleanroom experience of deposition technologies (CVD, ALD, EPI, PVD), hand-on assembly and testing experiences are strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
